# Files in the repository that are not part of the website. Everything here is
# already public on GitHub, so this is about keeping the deployed site to what
# a visitor should actually be able to fetch, not about hiding anything.
#
# Careful: anything listed here stops being served. Do not add data/, assets/,
# recipes/ or any .html, all of which the site fetches at runtime.

# The repository's own git history. wrangler does NOT skip this by itself: the
# assets directory is the repo root, so it walks .git too and the first deploy
# died on a 87.7 MiB pack file against the 25 MiB per-asset limit. This line is
# what makes the deploy possible at all, not tidiness.
.git/
.github/
node_modules/

tools/
api/
DEPLOY.md
wrangler.jsonc
worker.js
.assetsignore
.gitignore
CNAME
